# Line-ending policy for this repository.
#
# The repository index already stores everything as LF (confirmed with
# `git ls-files --eol`), but with no .gitattributes present, Windows clones
# with the (default) core.autocrlf=true converted every checked-out file to
# CRLF, including mvnw. Docker reads the working tree, not the index, so the
# build container looked for `/bin/sh\r` and failed with `./mvnw: not found`.
# These rules make checkout behavior explicit and platform-independent.

# Auto-detect text files and normalize their line endings in the repository;
# let Git convert to the platform's native ending on checkout otherwise
# (respects core.autocrlf). Covers Java, Markdown, XML, YAML, SQL, CSV,
# HTML/CSS and other plain-text/config files with no interpreter-path
# sensitivity, so no per-extension override is needed for them.
* text=auto

# Shell scripts and the Maven wrapper are executed by a POSIX shell (locally
# and inside the Linux Docker build context via `sh ./mvnw`), so they must
# always be checked out with LF, regardless of host OS.
*.sh text eol=lf
mvnw text eol=lf

# Windows batch/cmd scripts are only ever run by cmd.exe, which expects
# CRLF, so they must always be checked out with CRLF.
*.bat text eol=crlf
*.cmd text eol=crlf
